{"base_rate":0.334,"brier":0.072227,"bss":0.675302548057039,"bss_hi":0.7893255635607722,"bss_lo":0.5096176398296913,"chart":{"base":[495.1,56.7],"fp":[170.2,304.8],"lead":"62,207.6 272,204.8 482,194.9 692,185.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.68 — higher than 99% of cities","fp":"low end -1pp, high end +9pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.5 °C — better than 15% of cities","rel":"promised 6% → rained 3%; promised 100% → rained 95%"},"rel":"99.8,451.6 552.3,213.6 690.4,57.4"},"country":"GW","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.06194000000000003,"ess":62.057451005459875,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Bissau</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Bissau rain forecast is strongly skilful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>95%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 500 days, 2024-05-28 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 7.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.68, ranked 2 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(1&ndash;15) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>250</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'><b>20%</b></td><td class='num'>50</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>66%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>47</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>91%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>42</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>95%</b></td><td class='num'>111</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Bissau</b> <span class=\"muted\">GW</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.68</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>1&ndash;15\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>500 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Bissau &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Bissau\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\