% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 250 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"61.14352\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 32%&amp;#10;It rained 20% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 50 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"169.72240000000002\" cy=\"309.2\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 66%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 47 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"292.84510638297877\" cy=\"234.85106382978725\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 91%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 42 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"378.96\" cy=\"96.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 95% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 111 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.07513513513516\" cy=\"37.67567567567568\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(33%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p class=\"muted\">Not enough days in this city's record to split the year into four and still say anyth